---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Presbyterian Church Maui | Maui OPC"
  description="Looking for a Presbyterian church on Maui? We're planting one — elder-led, confessional, part of the Orthodox Presbyterian Church."
  canonical="https://reformedchurchmaui.com/presbyterian-church-maui/"
  h1="Presbyterian Church on Maui, Hawaii"
  breadcrumb={[{ name: 'Presbyterian Church Maui', url: 'https://reformedchurchmaui.com/presbyterian-church-maui/' }]}
>
  <p class="text-[#5F5E5A] text-base leading-relaxed mb-10">
    If you've been searching for a Presbyterian church on Maui, here's what that word actually means — and what we're building.
  </p>

  <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-[#1E2A3A] mt-10 mb-4">What makes a church "Presbyterian"?</h2>
  <p class="text-[#5F5E5A] leading-relaxed mb-8">
    "Presbyterian" describes how a church is governed, not just what it believes. A Presbyterian church is led by its session — the minister(s) and ruling elders together — who give oversight and provide pastoral care to the congregation. Local churches are also part of a broader assembly of elders, called a presbytery, providing accountability beyond the local church.
  </p>

  <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-[#1E2A3A] mt-10 mb-4">Are all Presbyterian churches the same?</h2>
  <p class="text-[#5F5E5A] leading-relaxed mb-8">
    Not exactly — there's a range of Presbyterian and Reformed denominations, each with its own history and practice. The OPC is part of NAPARC (the North American Presbyterian and Reformed Council), a fellowship of confessional Reformed and Presbyterian denominations that includes churches like the PCA and Reformed-but-not-Presbyterian churches like the URC. We're happy to talk through where we fit and answer any questions.
  </p>

  <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-[#1E2A3A] mt-10 mb-4">What to expect as a member</h2>
  <p class="text-[#5F5E5A] leading-relaxed mb-8">
    Being part of a Presbyterian church means real accountability in both directions — elders who know you and care for you personally, and a congregation that has a voice through its session. New members typically meet with the elders before joining, not as a formality but so the church actually knows who's part of it.
  </p>

  <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-[#1E2A3A] mt-10 mb-4">Planting a Presbyterian church on Maui</h2>
  <p class="text-[#5F5E5A] leading-relaxed mb-12">
    We are currently the only confessional Presbyterian church plant on Maui. For the full story of why that gap exists and what we're building to fill it, see <a href="/reformed-church-maui/" class="text-[#7A5F2A] underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-[#C4A35A]">Reformed Church Maui</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="border-t border-[#D3D1C7] pt-10">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
      <a href="/connect/" class="inline-block bg-[#C4A35A] text-[#1E2A3A] font-semibold px-6 py-3 rounded hover:bg-[#d4b36a] transition-colors">
        Get connected &rarr;
      </a>
      <a href="/what-we-believe/" class="inline-block border border-[#1E2A3A] text-[#1E2A3A] font-semibold px-6 py-3 rounded hover:bg-[#1E2A3A]/5 transition-colors">
        What we believe
      </a>
      <a href="/reformed-church-maui/" class="inline-block border border-[#1E2A3A] text-[#1E2A3A] font-semibold px-6 py-3 rounded hover:bg-[#1E2A3A]/5 transition-colors">
        Reformed Church Maui
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
